# Lifecycle fixture: timeout

Checked-in input for `test/wotex/lab/cookbook_runner_test.exs`, not a
cookbook. It leaves an unlinked process and a telemetry handler, reports
both to the test and then never finishes, so the runner must reclaim them
after its deadline.

```elixir
unlinked = spawn(fn -> receive do: (:release -> :ok) end)
handler = "lifecycle-timeout-#{System.unique_integer([:positive])}"
ignore = fn _event, _measurements, _metadata, _config -> :ok end
:ok = :telemetry.attach(handler, [:lifecycle_fixture, :timeout], ignore, nil)
send(observer, {:timeout_fixture, unlinked, handler})
```

```elixir
Process.sleep(:infinity)
```
